			<div class="content" id="post-content-2166679">
									

<p>Why not? Because when I get home from work and I start feeling numbness and pain I am not thinking about taking care of my pets. I am thinking about the heart attack I am having. I am thinking about where I left the asprin and if the house numbers are clear enough.</p>
<p>The EMT who sees the snake tank white his partner is intubating me is thinking &quot;Is that a real animal? How the hell is that thing still alive?&quot;</p>
<p>The animal control officer who arrives to pick up the snake and press animal cruelty charges is thinking &quot;Is this surgical? Who would do that to an animal?&quot;</p>
<p>The veterinarian filling out the report for the police knows something is very wrong. If the Foundation is lucky and careful they will catch her before she calls up other vets for a consult but probably not before photo documentation is on file at the police department and at least 30 people have called over their coworkers to say 'Hey look at this!'. Getting all those pictures off of instagram is going to be a headache.</p>
<p>Maybe at least add a note saying all snakes must be kept in an office on-site.</p>

